1013
01:11:03.921 --> 01:11:05.521
What is a distributed lock?

1014
01:11:05.801 --> 01:11:07.167
Thirty-second answer:

1015
01:11:07.447 --> 01:11:15.788
A lock shared by processes on different machines, so only one of them does something at a time, for example running tonight's settlement for a store.

1016
01:11:16.068 --> 01:11:23.428
It's usually implemented with a shared store (Redis SET NX with an expiry, etcd, ZooKeeper, or the database).

1017
